      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Two parallel neural ectoderm progenitors contribute to the developing brain",
      "url": "https://med.stanford.edu/news/all-news/2026/09/two-separate-brains.html",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49763697",
      "score": 633,
      "comments": 249,
      "author": "emigre",
      "published": "2026-09-19T05:48:50Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Nature study reveals dual parallel progenitor lineages build the brain, overturning classical linear, single-source neurogenesis assumptions.",
        "Mammalian brain architecture emerges from concurrent distinct embryonic stem streams rather than uniform, sequential neural differentiation.",
        "Provides biological grounding for multi-stream neuromorphic architectures and modular neural networks mimicking natural multi-pathway developmental processes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
