      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Software sandboxing: The basics (2025)",
      "url": "https://blog.emilua.org/2025/01/12/software-sandboxing-basics/",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/brptxb",
      "score": 4,
      "comments": 0,
      "author": "vinipsmaker",
      "published": "2026-09-20T14:13:11Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Modern Linux sandboxing leverages seccomp-bpf, Landlock, and cgroups to enforce granular syscall filtering and restrict process capabilities.",
        "Strong isolation models employ microVMs like Firecracker or sandboxed runtimes like gVisor to mitigate shared-kernel privilege escalation risks.",
        "WebAssembly runtimes, such as Wasmtime with WASI, offer lightweight, memory-safe user-space execution sandboxes without full hypervisor virtualization overhead."
      ]
    },
